<br class="ltx_break"><span id="S1.T1.3.7.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(2) Enumerate datasets and metrics.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S1.T1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Table 1</span>. </span><span id="S1.T1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">A comparison of our work with existing surveys on LLM unlearning. Most surveys focus on a larger or smaller scope than ours. Two surveys similar to ours focusing on LLM Unlearning adopt different classification criteria and lack detailed analysis on datasets and metrics.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2. </span>Backgrounds</h2>

<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1. </span>Machine Unlearning in LLMs</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Within the standard framework of machine unlearning, we consider a dataset <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and an <span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">original model</span> <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, parameterized by <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, trained on <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The subset of training data targeted for removal is denoted as the <span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">unlearn set</span> <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{u}\subset\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{u}\subset\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the remainder constitutes the <span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">retain set</span> <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}=\mathcal{D}\setminus\mathcal{D}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}=\mathcal{D}\setminus\mathcal{D}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The objective of machine unlearning is to design an algorithm <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math> that takes as input the original model <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and the relevant data, and outputs an <span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">unlearned model</span> <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This model <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is intended to approximate the behavior of a <span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">retrained model</span> <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is trained exclusively on the retain set <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.
An illustration of the unlearning process is provided in Figure <a href="#S2.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 2.1. Machine Unlearning in LLMs ‣ 2. Backgrounds ‣ A Survey on Unlearning in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
In the context of LLM unlearning, we provide specific explanations from two aspects: (1) different types of unlearning request and (2) the goal of unlearning.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S2.F1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="91.35" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 502.73 91.35" width="502.73"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,91.35) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(248.73,0) translate(0,-89.82)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -216.85 137.48)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.4em;--ltx-fo-height:3.4em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="40" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 40)" width="40"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><img src="2510.25117v1/figs/Survey.png" id="S2.F1.pic1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:40/40;" width="40" height="40" alt="Refer to caption"></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="1.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -152.59 127.95 L -241.11 127.95 C -244.93 127.95 -248.03 124.86 -248.03 121.03 L -248.03 115.19 C -248.03 111.37 -244.93 108.27 -241.11 108.27 L -152.59 108.27 C -148.77 108.27 -145.67 111.37 -145.67 115.19 L -145.67 121.03 C -145.67 124.86 -148.77 127.95 -152.59 127.95 Z M -248.03 108.27"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -242.91 95.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:6.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="9.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="81.35"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.F1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Original Model <math id="S2.F1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" stroke="#000000"><path style="fill:none" d="M -230.65 123.68 L -241.79 123.68 L -241.79 112.54 L -230.65 112.54 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" stroke="#000000"><path style="fill:none" d="M -210.97 123.68 L -222.1 123.68 L -222.1 112.54 L -210.97 112.54 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" stroke="#000000"><path style="fill:none" d="M -191.28 123.68 L -202.42 123.68 L -202.42 112.54 L -191.28 112.54 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" stroke="#000000"><path style="fill:none" d="M -171.6 123.68 L -182.73 123.68 L -182.73 112.54 L -171.6 112.54 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" stroke="#000000"><defs><pattern height="4" id="pgfpat3" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" width="4"><symbol id="pgfsym3"><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 L 4.29 4.29"></path></g><g></g><defs><pattern id="pgfupat9" href="#pgfpat3"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000"><use href="#pgfsym3"></use></g></pattern></defs><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:url(#pgfupat9);" fill="url(#pgfupat9)" stroke="#000000"><defs><pattern id="pgfupat10" href="#pgfpat3"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000"><use href="#pgfsym3"></use></g></pattern></defs><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000"><path d="M -151.91 123.68 L -163.05 123.68 L -163.05 112.54 L -151.91 112.54 Z"></path></g></g></symbol></pattern></defs></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -20 137.48)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.4em;--ltx-fo-height:3.4em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="40" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 40)" width="40"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><img src="2510.25117v1/figs/Survey.png" id="S2.F1.pic1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:40/40;" width="40" height="40" alt="Refer to caption"></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="1.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 44.26 127.95 L -44.26 127.95 C -48.08 127.95 -51.18 124.86 -51.18 121.03 L -51.18 115.19 C -51.18 111.37 -48.08 108.27 -44.26 108.27 L 44.26 108.27 C 48.08 108.27 51.18 111.37 51.18 115.19 L 51.18 121.03 C 51.18 124.86 48.08 127.95 44.26 127.95 Z M -51.18 108.27"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="1.0pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.48 113.79)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.47em;--ltx-fo-height:0.59em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10.65pt;" height="8.65" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="6.96"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.F1.pic1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">?</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -55.07 95.27)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:7.83em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:8.5pt;" height="7.69" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="92.12"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S2.F1.pic1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Unlearned Model <math id="S2.F1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g stroke-width="1.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -142.21 118.11 L -55.8 118.11"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="0.8pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -55.8 118.11)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.41 3.21 C -2.21 2.01 0 0.2 0.6 0 C 0 -0.2 -2.21 -2.01 -2.41 -3.21"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -137.7 136.33)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.11em;--ltx-fo-height:1.4em;--ltx-fo-depth:1em;font-size:10pt;" height="33.21" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 19.37)" width="70.7"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<table id="S2.F1.pic1.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S2.F1.pic1.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.F1.pic1.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><span id="S2.F1.pic1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Unlearning</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.F1.pic1.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.F1.pic1.4.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><span id="S2.F1.pic1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">algorithm </span><math id="S2.F1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.800em">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
