<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Figure 1</span>. </span><span id="S2.F1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Illustration of an unlearning process. The box below the model represents the composition of the corresponding training set. The unlearn set <math id="S2.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by the shadow square and the retain set <math id="S2.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by the white square. An unlearning algorithm is applying on the initial target model to obtain the unlearned model <math id="S2.F1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>. And the unlearned model is expected to approximate the retrained model <math id="S2.F1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S2.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">2.1.1. </span>Type of Unlearning Request</h4>

